  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n   We propose using a hierarchical Bayesian optimization framework to minimize the maximum overlap integral. The key innovation is employing multi-fidelity optimization by alternating between coarser and finer grids, while using Gaussian process surrogates to guide the search. This addresses the limitations of local optimization by:\n   - Maintaining a probabilistic model of the objective landscape\n   - Balancing exploration and exploitation\n   - Projecting to the feasible set (0\u2264h_i\u22641 and sum h_i dx=1)\n   - Using cheap-to-evaluate coarse grid surrogates to drive the search\n\n   The approach explicitly ensures:\n   - No gradient-based steps\n   - Careful interpolation between grid resolutions\n   - Separation of global and local search\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n   We minimize:\n      C5 = max_k \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\n   subject to:\n      h(x) \u2208 [0,1] for all x \u2208 [0,2]\n      \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1\n\n   Discretization:\n      Let hx be sampled over n evenly spaced points in [0,2] with dx=2/n\n      Objective: C5_dis = max_k (np.correlate(h,1-h,mode='full')*dx)\n\n   Representation:\n      h is represented as a 1D array of length n\n      We maintain n_0 = 400 as baseline, then 800, 1600, 3200, etc.\n\n   Optimization framework:\n      We use Bayesian optimization with:\n        n_initial = 10 initial evaluations per grid\n        GP surrogate modeling with automatic relevance detection\n        Expected improvement (EI) acquisition function\n        Box constraints [0,1] maintained by projection\n        No gradient computation\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   Function outline:\n      def run(budget_s):\n          import numpy as np\n          from sklearn.gaussian_process import GaussianProcessRegressor\n          from sklearn.gaussian_process.kernels import RBF, Matern\n          from scipy.optimize import minimize\n          from scipy.stats import norm\n          from scipy.optimize import gp_minimize\n          import time\n\n          def objective(h_vec, grid_level=0):\n              n = n_grids[grid_level]\n              # Ensure proper shape\n              if len(h_vec) != n:\n                  h_vec = np.clip(h_vec, 0, 1)\n                  while len(h_vec) != n:\n                      h_vec = np.random.rand(n)*0  # Force reproject later\n                  h = np.random.rand(n)\n              else:\n                  h = h_vec.clip(0,1)\n                  \n              # Check feasibility and repair if needed\n              if abs(sum(h)*dx - target) > 1e-5:\n                  h = project_feasible(h, target)\n\n              # Compute objective\n              corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n              return float(np.max(corr)) * dx\n\n          # Main strategy loop\n          t0 = time.time()\n          budget_remaining = budget_s\n\n          # Coordinator that plays three roles:\n          curated_solutions = {\n              400: project_feasible(np.array(initial_h_values), 200)\n          }\n          best_candidates = {400: curated_solutions[400]}\n          cur_grid = 400\n          best_value = objective(best_candidates[cur_grid])\n\n          # Cooldown schedule\n          phase_toggles = {\n              0: {'next_grid': 800, 'budget_frac': 0.6, 'cooldown': 10},\n              1: {'next_grid': 1600, 'budget_frac': 0.7, 'cooldown': 15},\n              2: {'next_grid': 3200, 'budget_frac': 0.8, 'cooldown': 100}\n          }\n\n          phase = 0\n          toggle_next = phase_toggles[phase]['next_grid']\n\n          # Selection and projection functions\n          def project_feasible(h, target):\n              # Adjust h to have integral = target (has dx factor implicit)\n              total = np.sum(h)\n              correction = target/total if total>1e-16 else 1\n              return np.clip(h*correction, 0, 1)\n\n          def gaussian_process_optimize():\n              n_dim = cur_grid\n              # Hypervolume bounds\n              space = [{'bounds': (0., 1.)} for _ in range(n_dim)]\n\n              # GP optimization\n              res = gp_minimize(lambda x: np.clip(x,0,1) * objective(x), \n                                space, \n                                n_initial_points=5,\n                                n_calls=phase_toggles[phase]['budget_frac']*budget_s,\n                                x0=None,\n                                y0=None,\n                                aquisition_function='EI',\n                                random_state=77)\n\n              return np.clip(res.x,0,1)\n\n          # Main optimization phase\n          while budget_remaining > 0 and time.time()<t0+30:\n              if cur_grid == toggle_next:  # Need to phase promote\n                  cur_grid = toggle_next\n                  phase += 1\n\n              # Sample from Bayesian kernel\n              try:\n                  new_h = gaussian_process_optimize()\n                  value = objective(new_h)\n                  if value < best_value:\n                      best_candidate = new_h\n                      best_value = value\n\n                  # Keep track of best for this grid\n                  curated_solutions[cur_grid] = new_h\n              except:\n                  # Cooldown and recovery\n                  pass\n\n              budget_used = time.time() - start\n              budget_remaining -= budget_used\n\n          n_final = cur_grid\n          final_h = project_feasible(best_candidates[cur_grid], n_final/2)\n          final_c5 = objective(final_h)\n\n          return final_h, final_c5, n_final\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n   - Grid progression: [400,800,1600,3200] dimensional scaling\n   - Initial: 5 points per configuration\n   - Hyperparameters:\n        Kernel: RBF(2.5) + Matern(1.0)\n        Acquisition: Expected Improvement\n        Bounds: Behavioural prioritization of boundary mutants\n   - Hybridization option:\n        Add local optimizer when moving between grids:\n          selector = sorted(feasible_candidates, key=lambda h: objective(h))\n         \u7cbe\u82f1\u4fdd\u7559\u6700\u4f18\u70b9\u8fdb\u884c\u5c40\u90e8\u4f18\u5316\n          n_local_moves = min(5, 2^(grid_size))\n   - Bi-level variation:\n        Primary: Bayesian optimization\n        Secondary: Differential evolution on feasible set\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n   - Time distribution:\n        \u30d5\u30a7\u30fc\u30ba0 (grid 400-800): 50% time budget\n        \u30d5\u30a7\u30fc\u30ba1 (grid 800-1600): 30% budget\n        \u30d5\u30a7\u30fc\u30ba2 (grid 1600-3200): 20% budget\n   - \u51b7\u5374\u65f6\u95f4:\n        Phase promotion requires at least:\n            \u8a13\u7ec3\u65f6\u95f4: len\u00b7t_size\u00b2/100\n        \u5982\u679cicer\u51b7\u5374\u7b49\u56e0\u7d20\u9884\u7b97\u4e0d\u8db3\uff0c\u6211\u4eec\u4f1a\u9009\u62e9\u66f4\u5c0f\u7684\u7f51\u683c\u3002\n   - \u7a33\u5b9a\u6027\u7b56\u7565:\n        \u6f02\u79fb\u68c0\u6d4b: \u5982\u679c\u4e09\u6b65C5\u6ca1\u6709\u540c\u6bd4\u4e0b\u964d\uff0c\u5219\u5207\u6362\u5230\u53cc\u7f51\u683c\u6a21\u5f0f\n        \u8fc7\u70ed\u7ba1\u7406: \u8d85\u8fc790%\u9884\u7b97\u65f6\uff0c\u6700\u5927\u5c3a\u5bf8\u56fa\u5b9a\u7f29\u5c0f80%\n        \u9ed2\u540d\u5355:\n               0 to1 -> 2 to3\n               400 to 400.1 ->\u964d\u81f3\u66f4\u5c0f\u7f51\u683c\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n   \u51fa\u529b\u68c0\u67e5:\n      1. \u8303\u56f4: (0 \u2264 all(h) \u2264 1)\n         integral = sum(h)*dx must match\n      2. \u76ee\u6807\u8bc4\u4f30:\n           \u5019\u9009\u8005 = project_feasible(\u8fd4\u56de\u503c, len(\u8fd4\u56de\u503c)/2)\n           score = max(np.correlate(candidate,1-candidate,mode='full'))*dx\n      3. \u8f93\u51fa\u683c\u5f0f:\n           (\u51b3\u8d5b_h_vectors, best_c5_score, n_points=len(betters))\n      4. \u5bb9\u9519 correction:\n           \u5982\u679c\u4efb\u4f55\u8bc4\u4f30\u4e2d\u65ad\uff0c\u53cd\u56de best_candidate\n           supernatural\u5904\u7406\u5305\u542b\u5c9b\u5c7f\u6a21\u5f0f\u548c\u4f20\u611f\u5668 \n           previous_phase +1",
